OL,3,ASetback for SpaceX Starship rocket's
OL,4,Adouble-catch test
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpaceX aborted its attempt to catch the
OL,7,Fbottom part of its huge Starship rocket
OL,8,Fduring its latest test flight.
OL,10,FThe aim was to catch it using the
OL,11,Fmechanical arms - nicknamed chopsticks
OL,12,F- on the launch tower as it returned to
OL,13,FEarth, but instead it was diverted to
OL,14,Fthe ocean, bursting into flames as it
OL,15,Fcame down.
OL,17,FThe top part of the rocket is now
OL,18,Fcontinuing its journey to space, and
OL,19,FSpaceX will decide whether it will try
OL,20,Fto catch this rocket stage at about
OL,21,F15:15 local time (21:15 GMT) on
OL,22,FSaturday.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,316,300,200,140,0,100
